 "answer": {
  "answer": "The goal was not met. Only two of the five cases the study aimed for were confirmed, each on a different scene. On 19f339ba, the policy failed in every run with the car on time, the car at 1.25x speed and the ego at 1.4x (S24). On 096988dd, it failed in every run with the car on time, the car at 1.25x and the ego at 1.2x (S3). The ranges for both settings lie above 0.5. A third candidate is 19f339ba with the ego at 1.2x (S23). It failed often, but its range still reaches below 0.5, so it is not confirmed.\n\nIn every confirmed failure, the ego's speed at hand-off was the knob that mattered. The policy was at fault each time, and none of the failures looks like a simulator artifact. The ego slowed (on 19f339ba it braked hard for no visible reason), drifted left against its route command, and hit a car passing in the left lane. That car was not the retimed one. The study barely varied the car's timing or speed, and the other eight scenes produced no failures in mostly single runs. So the study does not show which timing and car-speed combinations matter.",
  "findings": [
   {
    "claim": "Confirmed case 1: on 19f339ba, with the car on time, the car at 1.25x and the ego at 1.4x, every kept run collided. Each time the ego braked hard with no close lead, drifted left across the lane line and hit actor 1 as it passed in the left lane. The policy was at fault in all of them, with no possible artifacts.",
    "settings": [
     "S24"
    ]
   },
   {
    "claim": "Confirmed case 2: on 096988dd, with the car on time, the car at 1.25x and the ego at 1.2x, every run collided. The ego slowed in heavy traffic, drifted left even though the route said straight then right, and hit actor 41 alongside in the left lane. The policy was at fault in all of them.",
    "settings": [
     "S3"
    ]
   },
   {
    "claim": "On 19f339ba with the ego at 1.2x, the same left-drift collision with actor 1 happened in most runs. This is a strong candidate, but its range does not yet lie surely above 0.5.",
    "settings": [
     "S23"
    ]
   },
   {
    "claim": "On both failing scenes, the ego's speed at hand-off drives the failure, with the car's timing and speed held at 0 s and 1.25x. On 096988dd, the ego at 1.0x did not fail and the ego at 1.2x always failed. On 19f339ba, the failure rate rises from the ego at 1.0x to 1.2x to 1.4x.",
    "settings": [
     "S2",
     "S3",
     "S22",
     "S23",
     "S24"
    ]
   },
   {
    "claim": "The single failure on 19f339ba with the ego at 1.0x is a different kind of failure. After braking for no reason, the ego was struck by replayed actor 18 coming up from behind on the right. Triage could not say whether the policy was at fault, so this run is weak evidence.",
    "settings": [
     "S22"
    ]
   },
   {
    "claim": "The failures did not come from conflicts with the retimed car. In both failing scenes, the ego hit a different car in the adjacent left lane (actors 1 and 41) after slowing and drifting left. The failure mode is the policy's own unprompted braking and lateral drift, not a cut-in or a braking lead.",
    "settings": [
     "S3",
     "S23",
     "S24"
    ]
   },
   {
    "claim": "No failures were found on the other eight scenes in this search: 023b7fcc, 09a95ffa, 0cf6368d, 0dbb91dd, 0e899dd3, 12855a41, 187e6244 and 1c45ce3a. Most settings there have only one or two runs, which is a hint rather than a rate. 12855a41 held up in a few repeats at the ego 1.2x settings.",
